#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
cm - credential manager for pentest / CTF / OSCP|PNPT|CPTS engagements.

A single-file, stdlib-only tool for tracking usernames, passwords, hashes and
what you have done with them during an engagement. One SQLite database per
engagement boundary (e.g. standalone box, or an AD domain).

Design in one breath:
  * identities  (a WHO)  belong to a realm: a domain, a host, or a service.
  * secrets     (a WHAT) are passwords / hashes / key-blobs / tickets; unique
                 by (type, value) - the same secret found twice is ONE row.
  * identities <-> secrets links say who owns/uses what (origin, superseded).
  * secrets <-> secrets links say one secret cracks/unlocks another.
  * accesses say a (identity + secret) logs into a host or service, with a
                 status (untested/valid/invalid/expired) and a privilege.
  * observations record every place/way something was found (provenance).

Two command tiers:
  * everyday macros  : cred / works / fail / cracked / reset  (auto-upsert
                       everything, and echo the atomic steps they ran so you
                       learn the model).
  * atomic commands  : add / link / access / supersede / observe / unlock.

Run `cm --help` or `cm <command> --help`.
"""

